<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <string name="app_name">Easy Voice</string>

    <!--
      THE "POP-UP WINDOW" ANNOUNCEMENT, AND WHY IT IS ANSWERED HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE
      (owner, 2026-09-03: "drop down list open karne ke bad expand to announce
      karta hai TalkBack, but saath saath mein pop up window bhi announce kar
      raha hai ... pop up window ka uska code hata dena.")

      This is NOT our string and it was never in our code, which is why grepping
      the app for it found nothing. It belongs to androidx.compose.ui, and every
      Compose Popup, so ExposedDropdownMenu on the Voice and Mode settings
      screens and DropdownMenu on the Configuration rows, sets it as the title of
      the real Android window the menu lives in. From AndroidPopup.android.kt,
      createLayoutParams:

          // accessibilityTitle is not exposed as a public API therefore we set
          // popup window title which is used as a fallback by a11y services
          title = composeView.context.resources
                      .getString(R.string.default_popup_window_title)

      and in that library's own res/values/strings.xml the value is literally
      the words "Pop-Up Window".

      A screen reader speaks a window's title when the window appears, so opening
      any menu announced our own "Expanded" and then the library's "Pop-Up
      Window": two announcements for one action, which is what the owner heard.

      PopupProperties carries no title parameter. Checked against the pinned
      compose ui api/1.12.0-beta01.txt, its whole surface is focusable,
      dismissOnBackPress, dismissOnClickOutside, securePolicy,
      excludeFromSystemGesture, clippingEnabled, usePlatformDefaultWidth,
      windowType, windowToken, blurBehindRadius, scrimAlpha and nothing else, so
      there is no API knob to turn. Overriding the resource is the supported way:
      AAPT2 merges the application module's resources OVER a library's, so this
      value wins for every Popup in the app. Nothing is forked, no library code
      is copied, and no UI is hand written.

      It is EMPTY on purpose. The title has no useful content to carry, because
      the anchor already says "Expanded" and the reader then lands on the first
      menu item and reads it, so any wording here would be a second announcement
      of something the user has just been told. An empty title says "this window
      has no name", which is the truth.

      DO NOT delete this override to tidy up unused strings: it has no reference
      in our code by design, and a lint pass that removes it brings "Pop-Up
      Window" straight back.
    -->
    <string name="default_popup_window_title" tools:ignore="ExtraTranslation,UnusedResources"></string>
</resources>
